invariant: INV-16
file: sha512_avx2.c
catches: test/hash-builds.sh
reason: the target attribute of sha512_avx2.c's functions turns on BMI1 and
  BMI2 beside AVX2, and the compiler then writes RORX for the rounds'
  rotations. CH_CPU_AVX2 states AVX2 and no more: a caller reads it from
  the AVX2 bit of CPUID and from XGETBV, and a session whose CPU or
  hypervisor has AVX2 without BMI2 dies of SIGILL at its first SHA-384
  block. Every x86-64 runner CI draws has both, so every test that runs
  the kernel passes. The script compiles the file for x86-64 with the
  pinned clang and requires no BMI1 or BMI2 instruction in it, on every
  machine.

--- old
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((target("avx2"))), apply_to = function)
--- new
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((target("avx2,bmi,bmi2"))), apply_to = function)
